sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Dactylioceras commune Turing k_c at 24 µm (pass 1, stage 1) — MorphoEval overall 75.0/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 solves the Schnakenberg critical wavenumber so lambda_c is 24.19 µm (2.419e-05 m) at diffusion ratio 7.2, just above onset (6.724). Sigma at k_c is +0.0297. The stage-1 animation is a synthetic 44-rib coil, 12 frames at 640 px, computer-vision similarity 79.5 against the Whitby photograph. Pearson r of the dispersion curve, the equal-diffusion ablation, the diffusivity sweep, and the rib measurement on the real shell were not run. Overall 75.0/100 (faithfulness 71.1, reproducibility 84.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8c95fb91d41c76d640c8216d24030d8fd3768487; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 54, Morphometric validation 58, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 82. Output judged: datasets/dactylioceras_commune_turing_wavelength_s0/pass1_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 8c95fb91d41c76d640c8216d24030d8fd3768487, image/gif, 936417 B, 640×640 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 b8cc961dfa5bc20d66fbc7ca4a466125856246334d4a47e3cf6352e66af74666 (sha256 b8cc961dfa5bc20d66fbc7ca4a466125856246334d4a47e3cf6352e66af74666), spec_fingerprint 250d9efaee72b1c988aa7b69152735c73f811d95d1843ab2b2c5433409d97e1d. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 250d9efaee72b1c988aa7b69152735c73f811d95d1843ab2b2c5433409d97e1d; artifact_sha256: b8cc961dfa5bc20d66fbc7ca4a466125856246334d4a47e3cf6352e66af74666; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/dactylioceras_commune_turing_wavelength_s0/dactylioceras_commune_specimen.jpg=c309b077fb0c3b68..., datasets/dactylioceras_commune_turing_wavelength_s0/dactylioceras_commune_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=a8f717691a831459...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability at a finite critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979: activator-inhibitor kinetics a - u + u^2 v, b - u^2 v. | Catalogue slot: 24 µm detail scale, SI size 2.419e-05 m, Toarcian 181 Ma, D_f = 1.55. | James St. John, CC BY 2.0: Whitby Formation Dactylioceras commune, stated width 57 mm.; reconstructed_in_script: Du and Dv solved so k_c^2 = (Dv f_u + Du g_v) / (2 Du Dv) returns 2.419e-05 m. | Stage-1 synthetic fibulate coil used only as a first visual check.; transfer_boundary: Molluscan aperture pigment models are the transfer path onto an ammonite periostracum. Pass 1 does not test that transfer against the photograph.; does_not_claim: Pass 1 does not claim a dispersion-curve Pearson r, an ablation, a parameter sweep, or a rib measurement. | Pass 1 does not claim that 24 µm stripes are visible on the 57 mm shell. | D_f = 1.55 is a catalogue input, not a measurement on this photograph.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=3.0]: Dispersion Pearson r, RMSE, ablation, and specimen rib segmentation.",
            "open need [parameter_sweep/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=2.5]: Diffusivity scale sweep with monotonic lambda_c.",
            "remediation needed: R1 parameter-regime sweep: scale both diffusivities and show lambda_c moves monotonically.",
            "remediation needed: R2 negative control: equal-diffusion ablation must be stable at k_c while the Turing ratio is unstable.",
            "remediation needed: R3 real specimen CV segmentation: measure outer-whorl rib harmonic, rib spacing, coherency, and foreground on the Whitby photograph.",
            "remediation needed: R4 goodness-of-fit: Pearson r and RMSE of numerical versus analytical sigma(k), plus a KS test of orientations." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.75"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 builder-assessor, loop 3159 pass 1" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000> .
}

